# NestJS Clean Architecture

Applies to `backend/`. Overview also in `project-core.mdc`.

## Layers

```text
src/
├── domain/           # Entities, repository interfaces, value objects — no Nest/ORM
├── application/      # Use cases, ports, application DTOs
├── infrastructure/   # Drizzle, Redis, JWT, S3, repository implementations
├── presentation/http/# Controllers, guards, filters, HTTP DTOs
└── shared/           # Config, constants, cross-cutting helpers
```

**Dependency rule:** `presentation` → `application` → `domain` ← `infrastructure`

| Boundary | Allowed | Forbidden |
|----------|---------|-----------|
| Controller | Call use cases / application services | Call repositories or Drizzle directly |
| Use case | Ports (interfaces), other use cases sparingly | Import Drizzle/Nest HTTP |
| Domain | Pure TS | Nest, Drizzle, axios, env I/O |
| Infrastructure | Implement domain/application ports | Expose ORM entities as API DTOs |

## Use cases

- One use case ≈ one application action (`create-user.use-case.ts`)
- Validate input; enforce business rules; persist via ports
- Multi-write: run inside **one** DB transaction owned by the use-case (or a unit-of-work port). External payment/email side effects stay outside the tx when possible.

## Cross-module

- Orchestrate via application use cases / ports — not by reaching into another module’s repository implementation
- Do not query foreign tables from an unrelated repository

## Persistence

- ORM: **Drizzle** under `infrastructure/database/drizzle/`
- `synchronize: false`; migrations only
- Map DB rows ↔ domain entities inside infrastructure repositories

## REST

- Prefix `/api/v1`
- Controllers stay thin; Swagger on HTTP DTOs when present
- HTTP DTO = `createZodDto(SharedSchema)` from `@default/types`; class-validator is forbidden

```text
✅ UsersController → CreateUserUseCase → IUserRepository
❌ UsersController → Drizzle db.insert(...)
❌ Domain entity imports drizzle-orm
```
